EXPERIMENT 3: Implement Queue using Stacks (LC 232)

Aim:

To implement a Queue using two Stacks while maintaining the FIFO (First In First Out) property.

Algorithm:

1. Create two stacks: s1 and s2.
2. To insert (push) an element:
   a. Move all elements from s1 to s2.
   b. Push the new element into s1.
   c. Move all elements back from s2 to s1.
3. To remove (pop) an element:
   a. Store the top element of s1.
   b. Remove it from s1.
   c. Return the stored element.
4. To get the front element (peek):
   a. Return the top element of s1.
5. To check whether the queue is empty:
   a. Return true if s1 is empty; otherwise, return false.

Code:

class MyQueue {
public:
    stack<int> s1, s2;

    MyQueue() {

    }

    void push(int x) {
        while (!s1.empty()) {
            s2.push(s1.top());
            s1.pop();
        }

        s1.push(x);

        while (!s2.empty()) {
            s1.push(s2.top());
            s2.pop();
        }
    }

    int pop() {
        int store = s1.top();
        s1.pop();
        return store;
    }

    int peek() {
        return s1.top();
    }

    bool empty() {
        return s1.empty();
    }
};

/**
 * Your MyQueue object will be instantiated and called as such:
 * MyQueue* obj = new MyQueue();
 * obj->push(x);
 * int param_2 = obj->pop();
 * int param_3 = obj->peek();
 * bool param_4 = obj->empty();
 */

------------------------------------------------------------

Time Complexity:

Push: O(n)
Pop: O(1)
Peek: O(1)
Empty: O(1)

Space Complexity:

O(n)
